window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-cf38bd5054bede68"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"developer-commands\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">开发者命令</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"how-to-read-this-reference\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">如何阅读本参考文档</h2> <p>本页汇总了 Codex CLI 中所有有文档说明的命令和标志。你可以使用交互式表格按选项名称或说明搜索。每个部分都会注明功能成熟度，并标记已弃用的选项和有风险的组合。</p> <p>CLI 的大多数默认值继承自 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>。你在命令行传入的 <code>-c key=value</code> 会覆盖配置，仅对本次调用生效。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">配置基础知识</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"global-flags\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">全局标志</h2> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>globalFlagOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>这些选项适用于基础 <code>codex</code> 命令。大多数也会传递给子命令；例外情况请参阅上文说明或对应命令的帮助。对于会传递的标志，以相关命令帮助为准。例如，<code>codex exec --oss ...</code> 会将 <code>--oss</code> 应用于 <code>exec</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"command-overview\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">命令概览</h2> <p>“成熟度”列使用“实验性”“Beta”“稳定”和“已弃用”等功能成熟度标签。关于这些标签的含义，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-d303113c34a6b1a9\">功能成熟度</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>commandOverview</code></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"command-details\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">命令详情</h2> <p><a id=\"codex-interactive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex\"><code>codex</code>（交互模式）</h3> <p>不带子命令运行 <code>codex</code> 会启动交互式终端界面（TUI）。智能体接受上面的全局标志，也接受图像附件。网络搜索默认使用缓存模式；添加 <code>--search</code> 可切换为实时浏览。对于轻量的本地工作，可使用 <code>--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request</code>。</p> <p>使用 <code>--remote ws://host:port</code> 或 <code>--remote wss://host:port</code>，可连接到通过 <code>codex app-server --listen ws://IP:PORT</code> 启动的应用服务器。若要连接本地 Unix 套接字，可使用默认套接字 <code>--remote unix://</code>，或用 <code>--remote unix://PATH</code> 指定路径。如果服务器要求 WebSocket 身份验证令牌，请添加 <code>--remote-auth-token-env &lt;ENV_VAR&gt;</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app-server\"><code>codex app-server</code></h3> <p>在本地启动 Codex 应用服务器。它主要用于开发和调试，行为可能随时改变，恕不另行通知。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>appServerOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app-server --listen stdio://</code> 保持默认的 JSONL-over-stdio 行为；<code>codex app-server --stdio</code> 是这一传输方式的别名。<code>--listen ws://IP:PORT</code> 会启用 WebSocket 传输，供 app-server 客户端连接。服务器接受 <code>ws://</code> 监听 URL；若客户端通过 <code>wss://</code> 连接，请使用 TLS 终止或安全代理。使用 <code>--listen unix://</code> 可在 Codex 默认 Unix 套接字上接受 WebSocket 握手；使用 <code>--listen unix:///absolute/path.sock</code> 可指定套接字路径。若要为客户端绑定生成 Schema，请添加 <code>--experimental</code>，以包含受限功能的字段和方法。</p> <p>添加 <code>--code-mode-host wss://code-mode.example.com/host</code>，可让 app-server 连接远程 Code Mode 主机，而不是启动本地主机。这个出站连接与 <code>--listen</code> 相互独立，并由 app-server 进程中的所有线程共享。只有连接 localhost 或经 SSH 转发的主机时才使用 <code>ws://</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-remote-control\"><code>codex remote-control</code></h3> <p>运行 <code>codex remote-control</code> 时，符合条件的环境会通过受管后台服务器启动远程控制；若不可用，则退回前台模式。添加 <code>codex remote-control --no-daemon</code> 可明确要求以前台方式运行。运行 <code>codex remote-control start</code> 可启动启用了远程控制的本地 app-server 守护进程；运行 <code>codex remote-control stop</code> 可停止它。托管的远程控制客户端和 SSH 远程工作流使用这些命令；如果你正在构建本地协议客户端，它们不能替代 <code>codex app-server --listen</code>。</p> <p>守护进程启动后，运行 <code>codex remote-control pair</code> 可创建并打印一个短时有效的手动配对码。在任意远程控制命令后添加 <code>--json</code>，即可获取机器可读的输出。对于 <code>pair</code>，JSON 响应包含 <code>pairingCode</code>、<code>manualPairingCode</code>、<code>environmentId</code> 和 <code>expiresAt</code>。 <code>--no-daemon</code> 仅适用于不带子命令的 <code>remote-control</code>；不要将其与 <code>start</code>、<code>stop</code> 或 <code>pair</code> 组合使用。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-agents\"><code>codex agents</code></h3> <p>打开命令中心，浏览聊天并在共享服务器上切换智能体。使用 <code>--remote &lt;URL&gt;</code> 连接远程服务器，使用 <code>--cd &lt;DIR&gt;</code> 设置新远程任务的工作目录。<code>codex agents</code> 不支持 <code>--no-daemon</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-queue\"><code>codex queue</code></h3> <p>向已有会话排入一条文本消息：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex queue --thread &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --message \"Run the remaining checks\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--thread</code> 接受 UUID 或精确的会话名称。如果会话名称重复，请使用 UUID。此命令也接受 <code>--remote</code> 和 <code>--remote-auth-token-env</code>；不支持附加图像。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app\"><code>codex app</code></h3> <p>在 macOS 或 Windows 上从终端启动 ChatGPT 桌面应用。在 macOS 上，Codex 可以打开指定的工作区路径；在 Windows 上，Codex 会打印需要打开的路径。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>appOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app</code> 会打开已安装的 ChatGPT 桌面应用；如果尚未安装，则启动安装程序。在 macOS 上，Codex 会打开提供的工作区路径；在 Windows 上，安装完成后会打印需要打开的路径。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-app-server-send-message-v2\"><code>codex debug app-server send-message-v2</code></h3> <p>使用内置 app-server 测试客户端，通过 app-server 的 V2 线程/轮次流程发送一条消息。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>debugAppServerSendMessageV2Options</code></p> </blockquote> <p>此调试流程会通过 <code>experimentalApi: true</code> 完成初始化、启动线程、发送一轮对话，并流式接收服务器通知。可在本地用它复现和检查 app-server 协议行为。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-models\"><code>codex debug models</code></h3> <p>以 JSON 格式打印 Codex 看到的原始模型目录。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>debugModelsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>如果只想检查当前二进制文件中内置的模型目录，而不从远程模型端点刷新数据，请使用 <code>--bundled</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-prompt-input\"><code>codex debug prompt-input</code></h3> <p>以 JSON 格式呈现模型实际可见的提示输入列表。可用它调试指令发现、会话上下文或提示构造。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>debugPromptInputOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-apply\"><code>codex apply</code></h3> <p>将 Codex 云端聊天中最近一次生成的差异应用到本地代码仓库。你必须先完成身份验证，并且有权访问该聊天。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>applyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex 会打印已修改的文件；如果 <code>git apply</code> 失败（例如发生冲突），命令会以非零状态码退出。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-review\"><code>codex review</code></h3> <p>以非交互方式执行代码审查。请选择且只选择一个审查目标；也可以将自定义审查指令作为提示传入。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>reviewOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>--uncommitted</code>、<code>--base</code>、<code>--commit</code> 和自定义 <code>PROMPT</code> 不能同时使用。仅在使用 <code>--commit</code> 时才使用 <code>--title</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"codex-archive-and-codex-unarchive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-archive-codex-unarchive\"><code>codex archive</code> 和 <code>codex unarchive</code></h3> <p>根据会话 ID 或名称归档或恢复已保存的交互会话。若要整理会话选择器、但不删除对话记录，请使用这些命令。会话 ID 的优先级高于会话名称。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex archive &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>archiveOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-delete\"><code>codex delete</code></h3> <p>根据会话 ID 或名称永久删除已保存的交互会话。只有在确实要删除对话记录、而不是将其从活动会话列表中隐藏时，才使用此命令。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex delete &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex delete &lt;SESSION_UUID&gt; --force\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>deleteOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>仅在会话 UUID 上使用 <code>--force</code>。对于命名会话，仍需要确认，以免 Codex 未经提示就删除名称重复或含义不明确的会话。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-cloud\"><code>codex cloud</code></h3> <p>从终端与 Codex 云端聊天交互。默认命令会打开交互式选择器；<code>codex cloud exec</code> 会直接提交任务；<code>codex cloud list</code> 可返回近期聊天，供脚本调用或快速查看。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>cloudExecOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>身份验证使用与主 CLI 相同的凭据。如果任务提交失败，Codex 会以非零状态码退出。</p> <h4 id=\"codex-cloud-list\"><code>codex cloud list</code></h4> <p>列出近期云端聊天；可以选择筛选和分页。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>cloudListOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>纯文本输出会先打印任务 URL，再打印状态详情。自动化脚本可使用 <code>--json</code>。JSON 负载包含 <code>tasks</code> 数组和可选的 <code>cursor</code> 值。每项任务包括 <code>id</code>、<code>url</code>、<code>title</code>、<code>status</code>、<code>updated_at</code>、<code>environment_id</code>、<code>environment_label</code>、<code>summary</code>、<code>is_review</code> 和 <code>attempt_total</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-completion\"><code>codex completion</code></h3> <p>生成 Shell 补全脚本，并将输出重定向到合适的位置，例如 <code>codex completion zsh &gt; \"${fpath[1]}/_codex\"</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>completionOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-doctor\"><code>codex doctor</code></h3> <p>在提交支持请求之前，或调查 Codex 安装故障时，生成本地诊断报告。报告会检查安装、配置、身份验证、运行时、Git、终端、app-server 和线程清单的健康状况。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>doctorOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-features\"><code>codex features</code></h3> <p>管理保存在 <code>$CODEX_HOME/config.toml</code> 中的功能标志。<code>enable</code> 和 <code>disable</code> 子命令会持久保存更改，使其在后续会话中生效。<code>features</code> 子命令不接受 <code>--profile</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>featuresOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-exec\"><code>codex exec</code></h3> <p>对于需要以脚本或 CI 方式运行、且应在无人交互的情况下完成的任务，请使用 <code>codex exec</code>（或简写 <code>codex e</code>）。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>execOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>默认情况下，Codex 会输出格式化文本。添加 <code>--json</code> 可接收以换行符分隔的 JSON 事件（每次状态变化对应一条）。可选的 <code>resume</code> 子命令可以继续非交互式任务。使用 <code>--last</code> 可选择当前工作目录中的最近一次会话；添加 <code>--all</code> 可搜索所有会话：</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>execResumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>使用 <code>codex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; [PROMPT]</code> 可将已保存会话复制为新会话。会话参数接受 UUID 或名称。不提供提示时，Codex 会创建分支但不会开始新一轮对话。将 <code>-</code> 作为提示可从标准输入读取，也可添加 <code>--image</code> 附加图像。</p> <p>使用图像、<code>--output-schema</code>、<code>--output-last-message</code> 或 <code>--ephemeral</code> 时，必须提供提示。</p> <p>在新运行或分支运行中添加 <code>--worktree</code>，即可创建受管 Git 工作树：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec --worktree \"implement the next step\"\ncodex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree \"try an alternative approach\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--worktree</code> 要求在本地执行。不要将其与 <code>resume</code>、<code>review</code>、<code>--ephemeral</code> 或 <code>--ignore-user-config</code> 组合使用。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-execpolicy\"><code>codex execpolicy</code></h3> <p>保存规则文件前，先检查 <code>execpolicy</code> 规则。<code>codex execpolicy check</code> 接受一个或多个 <code>--rules</code> 标志（例如 <code>~/.codex/rules</code> 下的文件），并输出 JSON，显示最严格的判定和所有匹配规则。添加 <code>--pretty</code> 可格式化输出。<code>execpolicy</code> 命令目前处于预览阶段。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>execpolicyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-login\"><code>codex login</code></h3> <p>使用 ChatGPT 账户、API 密钥或访问令牌登录 CLI。如果不带任何标志，Codex 会打开浏览器并启动 ChatGPT OAuth 流程。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>loginOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>存在凭据时，<code>codex login status</code> 会以 <code>0</code> 状态码退出；这在自动化脚本中很有用。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-logout\"><code>codex logout</code></h3> <p>删除已保存的 API 密钥和 ChatGPT 身份验证凭据。此命令没有标志。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp\"><code>codex mcp</code></h3> <p>管理保存在 <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code> 中的 Model Context Protocol（MCP）服务器条目。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>mcpCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>add</code> 子命令同时支持 stdio 和可流式传输的 HTTP 传输方式：</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>mcpAddOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>OAuth 操作（<code>login</code>、<code>logout</code>）仅适用于可流式传输的 HTTP 服务器，并且服务器必须支持 OAuth。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin\"><code>codex plugin</code></h3> <p>从已配置的市场安装、列出和移除插件。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>pluginCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin add --json</code> 会打印 <code>pluginId</code>、<code>name</code>、<code>marketplaceName</code>、<code>version</code>、<code>installedPath</code> 和 <code>authPolicy</code>。<code>codex plugin list --json</code> 会打印 <code>installed</code> 和 <code>available</code> 数组。条目包括 <code>pluginId</code>、<code>name</code>、<code>marketplaceName</code>、<code>version</code>、<code>installed</code>、<code>enabled</code>、<code>source</code>、<code>installPolicy</code>、<code>authPolicy</code>；如果可用，还会包含 <code>marketplaceSource</code>，其中注明已配置市场源的类型和值。<code>codex plugin remove --json</code> 会打印 <code>pluginId</code>、<code>name</code> 和 <code>marketplaceName</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin-marketplace\"><code>codex plugin marketplace</code></h3> <p>管理 Codex 可浏览和安装插件的市场源。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>marketplaceCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace add</code> 接受 GitHub 简写（如 <code>owner/repo</code> 或 <code>owner/repo@ref</code>）、HTTP/HTTPS Git URL、SSH Git URL，以及本地市场根目录。使用 <code>--ref</code> 固定 Git 引用；对于基于 Git 的市场仓库，可以重复传入 <code>--sparse PATH</code> 使用稀疏检出。</p> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace list</code> 会打印当前适用范围内的市场名称和根目录，其中包括自动发现的默认市场和已配置的市场快照。</p> <p>在市场 add、list、upgrade 或 remove 命令后添加 <code>--json</code>，可获得便于自动化处理的输出。市场 add 的 JSON 包含 <code>marketplaceName</code>、<code>installedRoot</code> 和 <code>alreadyAdded</code>；list 的 JSON 包含 <code>marketplaces</code> 数组，其中含 <code>name</code>、<code>root</code> 和可选的 <code>marketplaceSource</code>；upgrade 的 JSON 包含 <code>selectedMarketplaces</code>、<code>upgradedRoots</code> 和 <code>errors</code>；remove 的 JSON 包含 <code>marketplaceName</code> 和 <code>installedRoot</code>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp-server\"><code>codex mcp-server</code></h3> <p><code>codex mcp-server</code> 命令和独立的 <code>codex-mcp-server</code> 二进制文件已被移除。请改用 <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app-server</a>。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-resume\"><code>codex resume</code></h3> <p>根据 ID 继续交互会话，或恢复最近一次聊天。除非传入 <code>--all</code>，否则 <code>codex resume</code> 只会在当前工作目录中查找 <code>--last</code>。它接受模型和沙盒覆盖设置，但不接受 <code>--worktree</code>。</p> <p>如果当前工作目录与会话保存时的目录不同，Codex 会询问要使用哪个目录。将 <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\"><code>tui.resume_cwd</code></a> 设为 <code>\"current\"</code> 或 <code>\"session\"</code>，即可在不提示的情况下采用相应选项。显式的 <code>--cd</code>（<code>-C</code>）覆盖优先于 <code>tui.resume_cwd</code>。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>resumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-fork\"><code>codex fork</code></h3> <p>将之前的交互会话分支为一个新聊天。默认情况下，<code>codex fork</code> 会打开会话选择器；添加 <code>--last</code> 可直接分支最近一次会话。</p> <p>如果当前目录与保存会话时的目录不同，<code>codex fork</code> 会使用与 <code>codex resume</code> 相同的工作目录提示和 <code>tui.resume_cwd</code> 设置。</p> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>forkOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>若要在受管 Git 工作树中分叉，请运行 <code>codex fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree</code>。此操作要求明确提供会话 ID，且必须在本地执行；不支持 <code>--last</code> 或会话选择器。</p> <h3 id=\"codex-sandbox\"><code>codex sandbox</code></h3> <p>使用沙盒辅助程序，在 Codex 内部相同的策略下运行命令。</p> <h4 id=\"macos-seatbelt\">macOS Seatbelt</h4> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>sandboxMacOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"linux-landlock\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"linux-sandbox\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"linux\">Linux 沙盒</h4> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>sandboxLinuxOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"windows\">Windows</h4> <blockquote> <p>配置表数据引用: <code>sandboxWindowsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-update\"><code>codex update</code></h3> <p>当已安装的版本支持自我更新时，检查并应用 Codex CLI 更新。调试版本会提示你改为安装正式发布版本。</p> <p><a id=\"flag-combinations-and-safety-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">标志组合与安全提示</h2> <ul> <li>对于无需人工干预、且可以限制在工作区内的本地任务，使用 <code>--sandbox workspace-write</code>。除非正在专用沙盒虚拟机中，否则避免使用 <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code>。</li> <li>如果需要允许 Codex 写入更多目录，优先使用 <code>--add-dir</code>，而不是强制设为 <code>--sandbox danger-full-access</code>。</li> <li>在 CI 中将 <code>--json</code> 与 <code>--output-last-message</code> 配合使用，以捕获机器可读的进度信息和最终自然语言摘要。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"interactive-shortcuts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">交互快捷键</h2> <ul> <li>输入 <code>@</code> 搜索工作区文件，并将其路径添加到提示中。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Up</kbd> 或 <kbd>Down</kbd> 恢复草稿历史记录。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> 搜索提示历史记录；然后按 <kbd>Enter</kbd> 使用匹配项，或按 <kbd>Escape</kbd> 取消。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>，或运行 <code>/copy</code>，复制 Codex 最近一次已完成的输出。</li> <li>在行首输入 <code>!</code>，可在当前审批和沙盒设置下运行本地 Shell 命令。</li> <li>Codex 工作期间按 <kbd>Tab</kbd>，可将后续提示、斜杠命令或 Shell 命令排入下一轮。</li> <li>Codex 工作期间按 <kbd>Enter</kbd>，可向当前轮次插入新指令。</li> <li>在输入框为空时连续按两次 <kbd>Escape</kbd>，可编辑上一条用户消息，并从该位置分支聊天。</li> <li>按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd>，或运行 <code>/exit</code>，关闭会话。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"related-resources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">相关资源</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI 概览</a>：安装、升级和快速提示。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础知识</a>：保存模型和提供方等默认设置。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">高级配置</a>：配置档案、提供方、沙盒调整和集成。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a>：了解 Codex 智能体功能及最佳实践。</li> </ul> <p>斜杠命令可以让你优先使用键盘快速控制 Codex。在输入框中输入 <code>/</code> 打开斜杠命令弹窗，选择一个命令后，Codex 就能切换模型、调整权限或总结长对话，无需离开终端。</p> <p>本指南会介绍如何：</p> <ul> <li>为任务找到合适的内置斜杠命令。</li> <li>使用 <code>/model</code>、<code>/fast</code>、<code>/permissions</code>、<code>/approve</code>、<code>/raw</code>、<code>/agents</code>、<code>/subagents</code> 和 <code>/status</code> 等命令控制正在进行的会话。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"built-in-slash-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">内置斜杠命令</h2> <p>Codex 附带以下命令。打开斜杠命令弹窗并开始输入命令名称，即可筛选列表。</p> <p>聊天正在运行时，可以输入斜杠命令并按 <code>Tab</code>，将它排入下一轮。Codex 会在命令执行时解析排队的斜杠命令，因此要等当前轮次结束后才会显示命令菜单和错误信息。排队前仍然可以使用斜杠命令自动补全。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>命令</th> <th>用途</th> <th>适用情形</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=update-permissions-with-permissions\"><code>/permissions</code></a></td> <td>设置 Codex 无需询问即可执行的操作。</td> <td>在会话中途放宽或收紧审批要求，例如在“自动”和“只读”之间切换。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=include-ide-context-with-ide\"><code>/ide</code></a></td> <td>纳入已打开文件、当前选区及其他 IDE 上下文。</td> <td>将编辑器上下文带入下一条提示，无需重新说明 IDE 中打开了什么。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\"><code>/keymap</code></a></td> <td>重新映射 TUI 键盘快捷键。</td> <td>查看并保存 <code>config.toml</code> 中自定义的快捷键绑定。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\"><code>/vim</code></a></td> <td>切换输入框的 Vim 模式。</td> <td>在 Vim 普通/插入模式和默认输入框编辑模式之间切换。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\"><code>/setup-default-sandbox</code></a></td> <td>设置提升权限的智能体沙盒（仅限 Windows）。</td> <td>Codex 提供提升权限沙盒设置时，用它替换受限的 Windows 沙盒。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=browse-apps-with-apps\"><code>/apps</code></a></td> <td>浏览应用（连接器）并将其插入提示。</td> <td>在提示中添加 <code>$app-slug</code>，然后让 Codex 使用该应用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=browse-plugins-with-plugins\"><code>/plugins</code></a></td> <td>浏览已安装和可发现的插件。</td> <td>检查插件工具、安装推荐插件或管理插件可用性。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\"><code>/hooks</code></a></td> <td>查看和管理生命周期钩子。</td> <td>检查已配置的钩子、信任新增或变更的钩子，或在执行前禁用非托管钩子。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=manage-chats-with-agents\"><code>/agents</code></a></td> <td>打开智能体命令中心。</td> <td>浏览聊天并在已连接的服务器上切换智能体。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\"><code>/subagents</code></a></td> <td>切换当前子智能体线程。</td> <td>检查或继续当前会话中的子智能体工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"><code>/clear</code></a></td> <td>清空终端并开始新聊天。</td> <td>需要重新开始时，同时重置可见界面和聊天上下文。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"><code>/rename</code></a></td> <td>重命名当前聊天。</td> <td>为已保存的会话设置容易辨认的名称，无需离开 TUI。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=archive-the-current-session-with-archive\"><code>/archive</code></a></td> <td>归档当前会话。</td> <td>将当前会话从活动列表中移除，但保留对话记录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=delete-the-current-session-with-delete\"><code>/delete</code></a></td> <td>永久删除当前会话。</td> <td>归档仍不够时，删除对话记录及其后代会话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\"><code>/compact</code></a></td> <td>总结可见聊天以释放 Token。</td> <td>长时间运行后压缩上下文，同时保留关键信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\"><code>/copy</code></a></td> <td>复制 Codex 最近一次已完成的输出。</td> <td>无需手动选择即可获取最新结果或计划文本；也可以按 <code>Ctrl+O</code>。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=review-changes-with-diff\"><code>/diff</code></a></td> <td>显示 Git 差异，包括 Git 尚未跟踪的文件。</td> <td>在提交或运行测试前检查 Codex 的修改。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/exit</code></a></td> <td>退出 CLI（与 <code>/quit</code> 相同）。</td> <td>两种写法都会结束会话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\"><code>/experimental</code></a></td> <td>开关实验性功能。</td> <td>启用网络代理或运行时阻止休眠等选项。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\"><code>/approve</code></a></td> <td>批准重试最近一次被自动审查拒绝的操作。</td> <td>重试被自动审查器拒绝的命令或操作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=configure-memories-with-memories\"><code>/memories</code></a></td> <td>配置记忆的使用和生成方式。</td> <td>在不离开 TUI 的情况下，启用或停用记忆注入或生成。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=use-skills-with-skills\"><code>/skills</code></a></td> <td>浏览并使用技能。</td> <td>选择相关本地技能，改进特定任务的处理方式。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\"><code>/import</code></a></td> <td>导入 Claude Code 或 Cursor 的设置。</td> <td>将受支持的外部智能体配置迁移到 Codex 配置和本地文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=send-feedback-with-feedback\"><code>/feedback</code></a></td> <td>向 Codex 维护者发送日志。</td> <td>向支持团队报告问题或提供诊断信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=generate-agentsmd-with-init\"><code>/init</code></a></td> <td>在当前目录生成 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 框架。</td> <td>为仓库或子目录记录持久指令。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=sign-out-with-logout\"><code>/logout</code></a></td> <td>退出 Codex。</td> <td>在共用电脑上清除本地凭据。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\"><code>/mcp</code></a></td> <td>列出已配置的 Model Context Protocol（MCP）工具。</td> <td>查看当前会话可调用的外部工具；添加 <code>verbose</code> 查看服务器详情。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=highlight-files-with-mention\"><code>/mention</code></a></td> <td>将文件附加到聊天。</td> <td>指定希望 Codex 检查的文件或文件夹。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=set-the-active-model-with-model\"><code>/model</code></a></td> <td>选择当前模型，并在可用时设置推理强度。</td> <td>如果列表中有 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 或 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>，可在开始任务前选择。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\"><code>/fast</code></a></td> <td>在模型目录提供快速服务等级时切换该等级。</td> <td>开启或关闭当前模型的快速服务，并保存选择。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\"><code>/plan</code></a></td> <td>切换到计划模式，可选择同时发送提示。</td> <td>在开始实施之前，请 Codex 提出执行计划。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\"><code>/goal</code></a></td> <td>设置、编辑、暂停、恢复、查看或清除任务目标。</td> <td>为较大的任务设定一个持续跟踪的目标。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=check-background-terminals-with-ps\"><code>/ps</code></a></td> <td>显示后台终端及其最近输出。</td> <td>无需离开当前对话即可检查长时间运行的命令。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=stop-background-terminals-with-stop\"><code>/stop</code></a></td> <td>停止所有后台终端。</td> <td>取消当前会话启动的后台终端任务。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\"><code>/fork</code></a></td> <td>将当前聊天分支为新聊天。</td> <td>保留当前对话，同时开辟分支尝试其他方案。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\"><code>/app</code></a></td> <td>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中继续当前会话。</td> <td>在 macOS 或 Windows 上从 CLI 切换到桌面应用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=start-a-side-chat-with-side\"><code>/side</code>、<code>/btw</code></a></td> <td>开始一个侧边聊天。</td> <td>针对某个问题临时分支讨论，不打断主聊天记录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\"><code>/raw</code></a></td> <td>切换原始滚屏模式。</td> <td>查看较长输出时，让终端选择和复制操作少受格式影响。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\"><code>/resume</code></a></td> <td>从会话列表恢复已保存的聊天。</td> <td>不开启新 CLI 会话，继续之前的对话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=start-a-new-chat-with-new\"><code>/new</code></a></td> <td>在同一个 CLI 会话中开始新聊天。</td> <td>在同一仓库中重置聊天上下文，而不退出 CLI。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/quit</code></a></td> <td>退出 CLI。</td> <td>立即离开当前会话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\"><code>/review</code></a></td> <td>请 Codex 审查工作树。</td> <td>Codex 完成工作后，或你想再检查一遍本地修改时使用。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=inspect-the-session-with-status\"><code>/status</code></a></td> <td>显示会话配置和 Token 用量。</td> <td>确认当前模型、审批策略、可写根目录和剩余上下文容量。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=view-account-usage-with-usage\"><code>/usage</code></a></td> <td>查看账户用量或使用已获得的限额重置。</td> <td>在 TUI 中检查 ChatGPT 的每日、每周或累计 Token 活动。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\"><code>/debug-config</code></a></td> <td>打印配置层级和要求诊断信息。</td> <td>调试优先级和策略要求，包括实验性网络约束。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=configure-footer-items-with-statusline\"><code>/statusline</code></a></td> <td>交互式配置 TUI 状态栏字段。</td> <td>选择并调整页脚中的模型、上下文、限额、Git、Token 和会话信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\"><code>/title</code></a></td> <td>交互式配置终端窗口或标签页标题。</td> <td>选择并调整项目、状态、线程、分支、模型和任务进度等标题信息。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\"><code>/theme</code></a></td> <td>选择语法高亮主题。</td> <td>预览并保存终端语法高亮主题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\"><code>/pets</code>、<code>/pet</code></a></td> <td>选择或隐藏终端宠物。</td> <td>使用内置宠物或自定义宠物个性化 TUI。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\"><code>/tui</code></a></td> <td>为下次启动选择终端模式。</td> <td>在终端滚屏记录和全屏对话记录之间切换。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=export-a-conversation-with-export\"><code>/export</code></a></td> <td>将对话导出为 Markdown。</td> <td>将完整转录保存到文件或复制到剪贴板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=summarize-the-chat-with-recap\"><code>/recap</code></a></td> <td>生成当前对话的摘要。</td> <td>不压缩上下文也能快速了解聊天内容。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/cd</code></a></td> <td>更改会话的工作目录。</td> <td>在其他目录中继续空闲的主聊天。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/pwd</code>、<code>/cwd</code></a></td> <td>显示工作目录。</td> <td>查看当前活动会话使用的目录。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\"><code>/worktree</code></a></td> <td>在受管 Git 工作树中开始或继续聊天。</td> <td>在本地仓库的独立检出中工作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\"><code>/daemon</code></a></td> <td>打开后台服务器控制。</td> <td>检查连接并管理由 Codex 管理的本地服务器。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=inspect-warnings-with-warnings\"><code>/warnings</code></a></td> <td>查看保留的警告和诊断信息。</td> <td>重新查看本次会话期间出现的警告。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><code>/quit</code> 和 <code>/exit</code> 都会退出 CLI。使用前请先保存或提交重要工作。</p> <p>使用 <code>/permissions</code> 调整 Codex 无需询问即可执行的操作。只有在需要重试最近一次被自动审查拒绝的操作时，才使用 <code>/approve</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"control-your-session-with-slash-commands\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">使用斜杠命令控制会话</h2> <p>以下工作流可帮助你在不重启 Codex 的情况下管理会话。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"tui\">使用 <code>/tui</code> 选择终端模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/tui</code>。</li> <li>选择滚屏记录或全屏模式，然后确认。</li> <li>重启 Codex 以应用所选模式。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：下次启动时会使用已保存的终端模式。<code>--no-alt-screen</code> 等启动覆盖项仍然有效。</p> <p><a id=\"export-a-conversation-with-export\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"export\">使用 <code>/export</code> 导出对话</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/export</code>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Copy to clipboard（复制到剪贴板）</strong> 或 <strong>Save to file（保存到文件）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将完整对话导出为 Markdown。若要直接保存到文件，请运行 <code>/export session.md</code>。导出前请等待当前轮次结束。</p> <p><a id=\"summarize-the-chat-with-recap\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"recap\">使用 <code>/recap</code> 总结聊天</h3> <ol> <li>Codex 空闲时输入 <code>/recap</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：即使 <code>tui.auto_recap = false</code>，Codex 也会生成对话摘要。若要释放上下文空间，请使用 <code>/compact</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"change-directories-with-cd\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"cd\">使用 <code>/cd</code> 切换目录</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/pwd</code>（或 <code>/cwd</code>）查看当前目录。</li> <li>输入 <code>/cd &lt;path&gt;</code> 切换目录；输入 <code>/cd</code> 则切换到你的主目录。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在所选目录中继续当前聊天。只有主会话空闲且没有排队输入或后台终端时，才可切换目录。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"worktree\">使用 <code>/worktree</code> 在工作树中继续</h3> <ol> <li>在本地 Git 仓库中输入 <code>/worktree</code>。</li> <li>选择开始新聊天，或在新的工作树中继续当前对话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会创建受管 Git 工作树，并在其中启动所选聊天。选择 <strong>Browse worktrees（浏览工作树）</strong> 可查找现有工作树及其所属聊天。此命令要求本地支持工作树，且任务运行期间不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"daemon\">使用 <code>/daemon</code> 管理后台服务器</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/daemon</code>。</li> <li>查看服务器连接状态和可用操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会提供安装最新公开稳定版，或使用当前 CLI 构建版本作为本地后台服务器的选项。确认更新后 Codex 会退出，并可能中断正在进行的工作。若连接的是远程服务器，请在其所在主机上管理服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-warnings-with-warnings\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"warnings\">使用 <code>/warnings</code> 查看警告</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/warnings</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示保留的警告及其诊断详情。</p> <p><a id=\"set-the-active-model-with-model\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"model\">使用 <code>/model</code> 设置当前模型</h3> <p>选择器只会显示当前账户和工作区可用的模型。如果列表中没有 GPT-6.1 Sol，请选择其他模型。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">各方案对 GPT-6.1 Sol 的访问权限</a>。</p> <ol> <li>启动 Codex 并打开输入框。</li> <li>输入 <code>/model</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>在弹窗中选择模型，例如 <code>gpt-6-luna</code> 或 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在对话记录中确认新模型。运行 <code>/status</code> 可验证设置是否生效。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"fast\">使用 <code>/fast</code> 切换快速模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/fast</code>，开启当前模型的快速服务等级。</li> <li>再次输入 <code>/fast</code>，关闭该等级。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换服务等级并保存选择。在 TUI 页脚中，也可以使用 <code>/statusline</code> 显示快速模式状态项。</p> <p>快速等级命令由模型目录决定。如果当前模型未声明快速等级，Codex 就不会显示 <code>/fast</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"plan\">使用 <code>/plan</code> 切换到计划模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/plan</code> 并按 Enter，将当前聊天切换到计划模式。</li> <li>可选：同时提供内联提示文字，例如 <code>/plan Propose a\nmigration plan for this service</code>。</li> <li>使用内联 <code>/plan</code> 参数时，也可以粘贴内容或附加图片。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会进入计划模式，并把可选的内联提示作为第一个计划请求。</p> <p>Codex 已在工作时，<code>/plan</code> 会暂时不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"goal\">使用 <code>/goal</code> 设置或查看任务目标</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/goal &lt;objective&gt;</code> 设置目标，例如 <code>/goal Finish the migration and keep tests green</code>。</li> <li>输入 <code>/goal</code> 查看当前目标。</li> <li>使用 <code>/goal edit</code> 修改目标；使用 <code>/goal pause</code>、<code>/goal resume</code> 或 <code>/goal clear</code> 分别暂停、恢复或移除目标。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在工作期间持续将该目标附加到当前聊天。</p> <p>目标内容不能为空，长度不得超过 4,000 个字符。如果指令较长，请将详细内容放进文件，然后在目标中指向该文件。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"experimental\">使用 <code>/experimental</code> 切换实验性功能</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/experimental</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>打开所需功能（例如网络代理或运行时阻止休眠）；如果 Codex 提示重启，请重启 Codex。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将功能选择保存到配置中，并在重启后应用。</p> <p><a id=\"approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"approve\">使用 <code>/approve</code> 批准重试被自动审查拒绝的操作</h3> <p>如果自动审查器最近拒绝了一项操作，而你希望 Codex 重试一次，请使用 <code>/approve</code>。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/approve</code>。</li> <li>Codex 显示相关被拒绝的操作后，确认重试。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会根据当前会话策略，对被拒绝的操作重试一次。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-memories-with-memories\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"memories\">使用 <code>/memories</code> 配置记忆</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/memories</code>。</li> <li>选择让 Codex 使用已有记忆、生成新记忆，或停用记忆功能。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新相关设置，以供后续会话使用。</p> <p><a id=\"use-skills-with-skills\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"skills\">使用 <code>/skills</code> 调用技能</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/skills</code>。</li> <li>选择要应用的技能。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会插入所选技能的上下文，使下一条请求遵循该技能的指令。</p> <p><a id=\"import-claude-code-configuration-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"cli-import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"import-claude-code-cursor\">使用 <code>/import</code> 导入 Claude Code 或 Cursor 设置</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/import</code>。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Claude Code</strong> 或 <strong>Cursor</strong>。</li> <li>选择要迁移的设置、项目文件或近期聊天。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开外部代理导入选择器，并将所选受支持资料导入 Codex 配置和本地文件。会话发现功能最多会包含最近 30 天内的 50 个聊天。</p> <p>请在本地 TUI 会话中运行 <code>/import</code>。任务正在运行时、处于远程会话中，或连接到本地 app-server 守护进程时，此命令不可用。</p> <p>关于桌面应用工作流和支持的资料类型，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-2b09a0f3c8670621\">从其他智能体导入</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"></a> <a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-task-with-clear\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"clear\">使用 <code>/clear</code> 清空终端并开始新聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/clear</code> 并按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会清空终端、重置可见对话记录，并在同一个 CLI 会话中开始新聊天。</p> <p>运行 <code>/clear release prep</code> 可以在新聊天创建时为它命名。</p> <p>与 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> 不同，<code>/clear</code> 会开始新聊天。<kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> 只会清空终端视图，并保留当前聊天。任务进行期间，Codex 会同时禁用这两种操作。</p> <p><a id=\"archive-the-current-session-with-archive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"archive\">使用 <code>/archive</code> 归档当前会话</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/archive</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>确认归档当前会话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：连接到本地后台服务器或远程服务器时，Codex 会归档会话并返回命令中心。未连接共享服务器时，Codex 会退出。Codex 会保留会话记录；稍后可通过 <code>codex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;</code> 恢复。</p> <p>如果当前轮次正在运行，确认 <code>/archive</code> 后，Codex 会先停止该轮次，再归档会话。</p> <p><a id=\"delete-the-current-session-with-delete\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"delete\">使用 <code>/delete</code> 删除当前会话</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/delete</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>确认删除当前会话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会永久删除会话记录及其派生的后代会话。连接到本地后台服务器或远程服务器时，Codex 会返回命令中心；未连接共享服务器时，Codex 会退出。</p> <p>聊天正在运行时或处于侧边聊天时，<code>/delete</code> 不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"update-permissions-with-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"permissions\">使用 <code>/permissions</code> 更新权限</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/permissions</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>选择符合你偏好的审批预设，例如无须逐项确认的 <code>Auto</code>，或可以检查编辑的 <code>Read Only</code>。启用具名权限配置时，选择器也会显示已配置的自定义配置及其说明。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会宣布更新后的策略。之后的操作会遵循新审批模式，直到你再次更改。</p> <p><a id=\"include-ide-context-with-ide\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"ide-ide\">使用 <code>/ide</code> 纳入 IDE 上下文</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/ide</code>。</li> <li>如果希望 Codex 如何处理当前 IDE 选区或已打开文件，可选地添加内联文字说明。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在下一条提示中加入可用的 IDE 上下文。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"vim-vim\">使用 <code>/vim</code> 切换 Vim 模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/vim</code>。</li> <li>在输入框中继续编辑。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换本次会话的输入框 Vim 模式。若要将 Vim 模式设为新会话的默认值，请在 <code>config.toml</code> 中设置 <code>tui.vim_mode_default = true</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"setup-default-sandbox-windows\">使用 <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code> 设置提升权限的 Windows 沙盒</h3> <p>只有当 Codex 在 Windows 上使用受限令牌沙盒（功能受限的沙盒）时，才会显示此命令。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code>。</li> <li>按照管理员设置流程操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会配置提升权限的 Windows 沙盒，并选择相应的自动审批预设。</p> <p><a id=\"copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"copy\">使用 <code>/copy</code> 复制最近一次回复</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/copy</code> 并按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将最近一次已完成的 Codex 输出复制到剪贴板。</p> <p>如果某一轮仍在运行，<code>/copy</code> 会使用最近一次已完成的输出，而不是尚未完成的回复。首次获得已完成输出之前以及回滚之后，此命令不可用。</p> <p>也可以在主 TUI 中按 <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd>，无需打开斜杠命令菜单即可复制最近一次已完成的回复。</p> <p><a id=\"toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"raw\">使用 <code>/raw</code> 切换原始滚屏模式</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/raw</code>、<code>/raw on</code> 或 <code>/raw off</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换原始滚屏模式，使终端选择和复制操作更直接。你也可以使用默认快捷键 <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd>，或将 <code>tui.raw_output_mode = true</code> 写入配置以保存默认设置。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-the-session-with-status\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"status\">使用 <code>/status</code> 检查会话</h3> <ol> <li>在任意聊天中输入 <code>/status</code>。</li> <li>检查输出中的当前模型、审批策略、可写根目录和 Token 用量。TUI 远程连接时，输出还会显示远程地址和服务器版本。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打印摘要，确认它正在按预期运行。</p> <p><a id=\"view-account-usage-with-usage\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"usage\">使用 <code>/usage</code> 查看账户用量</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/usage</code> 打开用量菜单。</li> <li>选择查看 Token 活动，或兑换可用的已获得重置额度。</li> <li>若要直接打开 Token 活动，可输入 <code>/usage daily</code>、<code>/usage weekly</code> 或 <code>/usage cumulative</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开用量操作，或显示所选视图的账户 Token 活动。如果会话未使用 Codex 服务账户身份验证，Codex 会提示需要登录。</p> <p><a id=\"inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"debug-config\">使用 <code>/debug-config</code> 检查配置层</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/debug-config</code>。</li> <li>检查配置层顺序（优先级从低到高）、开关状态和策略来源。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打印配置层诊断信息，以及已配置时的 <code>allowed_approval_policies</code>、<code>allowed_sandbox_modes</code>、<code>mcp_servers</code>、<code>rules</code> 和 <code>experimental_network</code> 等策略详情。</p> <p>可以利用这些输出排查有效设置为何与 <code>config.toml</code> 中的值不同。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-footer-items-with-statusline\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"statusline\">使用 <code>/statusline</code> 配置页脚信息</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/statusline</code>。</li> <li>在选择器中开关或调整项目顺序，然后确认。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：页脚状态栏会立即更新，并将设置保存到 <code>config.toml</code> 的 <code>tui.status_line</code> 中。</p> <p>可选状态栏项目包括模型、模型与推理强度、上下文统计、限额、Git 分支、Token 计数器、会话 ID、当前目录/项目根目录和 Codex 版本。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"title\">使用 <code>/title</code> 配置终端标题</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/title</code>。</li> <li>在选择器中开关或调整项目顺序，然后确认。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：终端窗口或标签页标题会立即更新，并将设置保存到 <code>config.toml</code> 的 <code>tui.terminal_title</code> 中。</p> <p>可选标题项目包括应用名称、项目、旋转指示器、状态、线程、Git 分支、模型和任务进度。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"theme\">使用 <code>/theme</code> 选择语法主题</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/theme</code>。</li> <li>在选择器中预览主题，然后确认。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新语法高亮，并将选择保存到 <code>config.toml</code> 的 <code>tui.theme</code> 中。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"pets\">使用 <code>/pets</code> 选择终端宠物</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/pets</code>（或 <code>/pet</code>）打开宠物选择器。</li> <li>选择内置或自定义宠物，也可以关闭宠物。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在支持的终端中显示所选的环境宠物，并保存选择。也可以输入 <code>/pets off</code> 隐藏宠物。</p> <p><a id=\"remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"keymap-tui\">使用 <code>/keymap</code> 重新映射 TUI 快捷键</h3> <p>使用 <code>/keymap</code> 查看、更新和保存 TUI 键盘快捷键绑定。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/keymap</code>。</li> <li>选择要更改的快捷键上下文和操作。</li> <li>输入新的绑定，或移除现有绑定。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新活动快捷键映射，并将自定义绑定写入 <code>config.toml</code> 的 <code>tui.keymap</code>。</p> <p>快捷键名称示例：<code>ctrl-a</code>、<code>shift-enter</code> 和 <code>page-down</code>。特定上下文的绑定会覆盖 <code>tui.keymap.global</code>；空绑定列表会解除该操作的绑定。</p> <p><a id=\"check-background-terminals-with-ps\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"ps\">使用 <code>/ps</code> 检查后台终端</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/ps</code>。</li> <li>查看后台终端及其状态列表。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示每个后台终端的命令，以及最多三行近期非空输出，方便你快速判断进度。</p> <p>仅在使用 <code>unified_exec</code> 时才会出现后台终端；否则列表可能为空。</p> <p><a id=\"stop-background-terminals-with-stop\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"stop\">使用 <code>/stop</code> 停止后台终端</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/stop</code>。</li> <li>如果 Codex 要求确认，请确认停止列出的终端。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会停止当前会话的所有后台终端。<code>/clean</code> 仍可作为 <code>/stop</code> 的别名使用。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"compact\">使用 <code>/compact</code> 精简对话记录</h3> <ol> <li>经过较长对话后，输入 <code>/compact</code>。</li> <li>Codex 提示总结到目前为止的聊天时，确认操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会用简洁摘要替换较早的轮次，在保留关键信息的同时释放上下文空间。</p> <p><a id=\"review-changes-with-diff\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"diff\">使用 <code>/diff</code> 审查修改</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/diff</code> 查看 Git 差异。</li> <li>在 CLI 中滚动查看输出，检查修改和新增文件。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示已暂存、尚未暂存，以及 Git 尚未开始跟踪的文件更改，供你决定如何处理。</p> <p><a id=\"highlight-files-with-mention\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"mention\">使用 <code>/mention</code> 标记文件</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/mention</code> 和路径，例如 <code>/mention src/lib/api.ts</code>。</li> <li>在弹窗中选择匹配结果。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将文件添加到聊天中，确保后续轮次会直接引用该文件。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-new-conversation-with-new\"></a> <a id=\"start-a-new-chat-with-new\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"new\">使用 <code>/new</code> 开始新聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/new</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>如果 Codex 提供工作树选项，请选择当前目录或新建工作树。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在同一 CLI 会话中开始新聊天，让你无需离开终端即可切换聊天。</p> <p>运行 <code>/new bug bash</code> 可在创建新聊天时为它命名。</p> <p>与 <code>/clear</code> 不同，<code>/new</code> 不会先清空当前终端视图。</p> <p><a id=\"rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"></a> <a id=\"rename-the-current-task-with-rename\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"rename\">使用 <code>/rename</code> 重命名当前聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/rename &lt;name&gt;</code>，或只输入 <code>/rename</code> 打开命名提示。</li> <li>输入一个简短名称，方便以后找到此聊天。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会更新已保存聊天的名称，但不会更改对话记录。</p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-saved-conversation-with-resume\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"resume\">使用 <code>/resume</code> 恢复已保存的聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/resume</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>在已保存会话选择器中选择要恢复的会话。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会重新载入所选聊天的对话记录，让你从上次中断处继续，同时保留原有历史。</p> <p><a id=\"fork-the-current-conversation-with-fork\"></a> <a id=\"fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"fork\">使用 <code>/fork</code> 分支当前聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/fork</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>如果 Codex 提供工作树选项，请选择当前目录或新建工作树。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会将当前聊天复制为一个拥有新 ID 的聊天，同时保持原对话记录不变，让你可以并行探索其他方案。</p> <p>如果要分支已保存的会话，而不是当前会话，请在终端运行 <code>codex fork</code> 打开会话选择器。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"app\">使用 <code>/app</code> 在桌面应用中继续</h3> <p>在 macOS 或 Windows 上输入 <code>/app</code>，可在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开当前会话。如果应用尚未安装或正在运行，Codex 会提示你安装或启动应用。</p> <p>预期结果：桌面应用会打开同一个已保存聊天，你可以在那里继续。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-side-conversation-with-side\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-side-chat-with-side\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"side\">使用 <code>/side</code> 开始侧边聊天</h3> <p>使用 <code>/side</code> 可从当前聊天临时分支出一个侧边聊天，同时不离开主聊天。</p> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/side</code> 开启侧边聊天。</li> <li>可选：添加内联文字，例如 <code>/side Check whether this plan has an obvious risk</code>。</li> <li>完成这次聚焦讨论后，返回父聊天。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开一个与父聊天记录分开的侧边聊天。处于侧边模式时，TUI 仍会显示父聊天状态，方便你确认主聊天是否仍在运行。</p> <p>处于另一个侧边聊天或审查模式时，<code>/side</code> 不可用。</p> <p><a id=\"generate-agentsmd-with-init\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"init-agentsmd\">使用 <code>/init</code> 生成 <code>AGENTS.md</code></h3> <ol> <li>在你希望 Codex 查找持久指令的目录中运行 <code>/init</code>。</li> <li>检查生成的 <code>AGENTS.md</code>，再根据仓库规范编辑它。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会创建 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 框架，你可以完善内容并提交，以供后续会话使用。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"review\">使用 <code>/review</code> 审查工作树</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/review</code>。</li> <li>如果想检查具体文件更改，可再运行 <code>/diff</code>。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会汇总工作树中发现的问题，重点关注行为变化和缺失测试。除非在 <code>config.toml</code> 中设置了 <code>review_model</code>，否则使用当前会话模型。</p> <p><a id=\"list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"mcp-mcp\">使用 <code>/mcp</code> 列出 MCP 工具</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/mcp</code>。</li> <li>检查列表，确认当前会话可以使用哪些 MCP 服务器和工具。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：你会看到本次会话中 Codex 可以调用的已配置 Model Context Protocol（MCP）工具。</p> <p>使用 <code>/mcp verbose</code> 可查看详细服务器诊断信息。使用 <code>/mcp login &lt;name&gt;</code> 可在当前会话中登录已配置的 MCP 服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"browse-apps-with-apps\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"apps\">使用 <code>/apps</code> 浏览应用</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/apps</code>。</li> <li>从列表中选择一个应用。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会在输入框中插入应用提及 <code>$app-slug</code>，你可以立即要求 Codex 使用它。</p> <p><a id=\"browse-plugins-with-plugins\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"plugins\">使用 <code>/plugins</code> 浏览插件</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/plugins</code>。</li> <li>选择一个市场标签页，再选择插件查看其功能或可用操作。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开插件浏览器，让你检查已安装插件、配置允许发现的插件，以及插件的已安装状态。对已安装插件按 <kbd>Space</kbd> 可切换启用状态。</p> <p><a id=\"view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"hooks\">使用 <code>/hooks</code> 查看和管理生命周期钩子</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/hooks</code>。</li> <li>选择一个钩子事件，查看匹配的处理程序。</li> <li>根据需要信任、禁用或重新启用非托管钩子。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会打开钩子浏览器，让你检查已配置的生命周期钩子。托管钩子会标记为托管，无法从用户钩子浏览器中禁用。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-chats-with-agents\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"agents\">使用 <code>/agents</code> 管理聊天</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/agents</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>在命令中心选择一条聊天以打开。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会显示已连接服务器上的聊天概览。你可以查看聊天状态并在聊天之间切换。若要直接从终端打开命令中心，请运行 <code>codex agents</code>。命令中心需要共享的本地或远程服务器。</p> <p><a id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-agent\"></a> <a id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"subagents\">使用 <code>/subagents</code> 切换智能体线程</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/subagents</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>在选择器中选取要切换到的线程。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会切换到所选活动线程，让你检查或继续该智能体的工作。</p> <p><a id=\"send-feedback-with-feedback\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"feedback\">使用 <code>/feedback</code> 发送反馈</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/feedback</code> 并按 Enter。</li> <li>按提示选择是否附上日志或诊断信息。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会收集所需诊断信息并提交给维护者。</p> <p><a id=\"sign-out-with-logout\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"logout\">使用 <code>/logout</code> 退出登录</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/logout</code> 并按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会清除当前用户会话的本地凭据。</p> <p><a id=\"exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"quit-exit-cli\">使用 <code>/quit</code> 或 <code>/exit</code> 退出 CLI</h3> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/quit</code>（或 <code>/exit</code>）并按 Enter。</li> </ol> <p>预期结果：Codex 会立即退出。请先保存或提交重要工作。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"developer-commands\">Developer commands</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"how-to-read-this-reference\">How to read this reference</h2> <p>This page catalogs every documented Codex CLI command and flag. Use the interactive tables to search by key or description. Each section shows the option's maturity and flags deprecated options and risky combinations.</p> <p>The CLI inherits most defaults from <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>. Any <code>-c key=value</code> overrides you pass at the command line take precedence for that invocation. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">Config basics</a> for more information.</p> <h2 id=\"global-flags\">Global flags</h2> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>globalFlagOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>These options apply to the base <code>codex</code> command. Most propagate to commands; see the notes above or the relevant command help for exceptions. For propagated flags, follow the relevant command help. For example, <code>codex exec --oss ...</code> applies <code>--oss</code> to <code>exec</code>.</p> <h2 id=\"command-overview\">Command overview</h2> <p>The Maturity column uses feature maturity labels such as Experimental, Beta, Stable, and Deprecated. See <a href=\"#/article/a-d303113c34a6b1a9\">Feature Maturity</a> for how to interpret these labels.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>commandOverview</code></p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"command-details\">Command details</h2> <h3 id=\"codex-interactive\"><code>codex</code> (interactive)</h3> <p>Running <code>codex</code> with no subcommand launches the interactive terminal UI (TUI). The agent accepts the global flags above plus image attachments. Web search defaults to cached mode; use <code>--search</code> to switch to live browsing. For low-friction local work, use <code>--sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval on-request</code>.</p> <p>Use <code>--remote ws://host:port</code> or <code>--remote wss://host:port</code> to connect the TUI to an app server started with <code>codex app-server --listen ws://IP:PORT</code>. For a local Unix socket, use <code>--remote unix://</code> for the default socket or <code>--remote unix://PATH</code> for an explicit path. Add <code>--remote-auth-token-env &lt;ENV_VAR&gt;</code> when the server requires a bearer token for WebSocket authentication.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-agents\"><code>codex agents</code></h3> <p>Open the command center to browse chats and switch between agents on a shared server. Use <code>--remote &lt;URL&gt;</code> to connect to a remote server and <code>--cd &lt;DIR&gt;</code> to set the directory for new remote tasks. <code>codex agents</code> doesn't support <code>--no-daemon</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-queue\"><code>codex queue</code></h3> <p>Queue a text message for an existing session:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex queue --thread &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --message \"Run the remaining checks\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--thread</code> accepts a UUID or exact session name. Use a UUID when sessions share the same name. The command also accepts <code>--remote</code> and <code>--remote-auth-token-env</code>; image attachments aren't supported.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app-server\"><code>codex app-server</code></h3> <p>Launch the Codex app server locally. This is primarily for development and debugging and may change without notice.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>appServerOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app-server --listen stdio://</code> keeps the default JSONL-over-stdio behavior, and <code>codex app-server --stdio</code> is an alias for that transport. <code>--listen ws://IP:PORT</code> enables WebSocket transport for app-server clients. The server accepts <code>ws://</code> listen URLs; use TLS termination or a secure proxy when clients connect with <code>wss://</code>. Use <code>--listen unix://</code> to accept WebSocket handshakes on Codex's default Unix socket, or <code>--listen unix:///absolute/path.sock</code> to choose a socket path. If you generate schemas for client bindings, add <code>--experimental</code> to include gated fields and methods.</p> <p>Add <code>--code-mode-host wss://code-mode.example.com/host</code> to connect app-server to a remote Code Mode host instead of starting a local host. This outbound connection is separate from <code>--listen</code> and shared by every thread in the app-server process. Use <code>ws://</code> only for a localhost or SSH-forwarded host.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-remote-control\"><code>codex remote-control</code></h3> <p>Run <code>codex remote-control</code> to start remote control through the managed background server when eligible, with a foreground fallback. Use <code>codex remote-control --no-daemon</code> to run in the foreground explicitly. Use <code>codex remote-control start</code> to start the local app-server daemon with remote control enabled, and <code>codex remote-control stop</code> to stop it. Managed remote-control clients and SSH remote workflows use these commands; they aren't a replacement for <code>codex app-server --listen</code> when you're building a local protocol client.</p> <p>After the daemon is running, use <code>codex remote-control pair</code> to create and print a short-lived manual pairing code. Add <code>--json</code> to any remote-control command for machine-readable output. For <code>pair</code>, the JSON response includes <code>pairingCode</code>, <code>manualPairingCode</code>, <code>environmentId</code>, and <code>expiresAt</code>. <code>--no-daemon</code> applies only to the bare <code>remote-control</code> command; don't combine it with <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, or <code>pair</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-app\"><code>codex app</code></h3> <p>Launch the ChatGPT desktop app from the terminal on macOS or Windows. On macOS, Codex can open a specific workspace path; on Windows, Codex prints the path to open.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>appOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex app</code> opens an installed ChatGPT desktop app, or starts the installer when the app is missing. On macOS, Codex opens the provided workspace path; on Windows, it prints the path to open after installation.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-app-server-send-message-v2\"><code>codex debug app-server send-message-v2</code></h3> <p>Send one message through app-server's V2 thread/turn flow using the built-in app-server test client.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>debugAppServerSendMessageV2Options</code></p> </blockquote> <p>This debug flow initializes with <code>experimentalApi: true</code>, starts a thread, sends a turn, and streams server notifications. Use it to reproduce and inspect app-server protocol behavior locally.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-models\"><code>codex debug models</code></h3> <p>Print the raw model catalog Codex sees as JSON.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>debugModelsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>--bundled</code> when you want to inspect only the catalog bundled with the current binary, without refreshing from the remote models endpoint.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-debug-prompt-input\"><code>codex debug prompt-input</code></h3> <p>Render the exact model-visible prompt input list as JSON. Use this when debugging instruction discovery, session context, or prompt construction.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>debugPromptInputOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-apply\"><code>codex apply</code></h3> <p>Apply the most recent diff from a Codex cloud chat to your local repository. You must authenticate and have access to the chat.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>applyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex prints the patched files and exits non-zero if <code>git apply</code> fails (for example, due to conflicts).</p> <h3 id=\"codex-review\"><code>codex review</code></h3> <p>Run a code review non-interactively. Choose exactly one review target, or pass custom review instructions as a prompt.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>reviewOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>--uncommitted</code>, <code>--base</code>, <code>--commit</code>, and a custom <code>PROMPT</code> conflict with one another. Use <code>--title</code> only with <code>--commit</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-archive-and-codex-unarchive\"><code>codex archive</code> and <code>codex unarchive</code></h3> <p>Archive or restore a saved interactive session by session ID or session name. Use these commands when you want to clean up the session picker without deleting the transcript. Session IDs take precedence over session names.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex archive &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>archiveOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-delete\"><code>codex delete</code></h3> <p>Permanently delete a saved interactive session by session ID or session name. Use this only when you want to remove the transcript instead of hiding it from active session lists.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex delete &lt;SESSION&gt;\ncodex delete &lt;SESSION_UUID&gt; --force\n</code></pre> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>deleteOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>--force</code> only with a session UUID. Named sessions still require confirmation so Codex doesn't delete a repeated or ambiguous name without a prompt.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-cloud\"><code>codex cloud</code></h3> <p>Interact with Codex cloud chats from the terminal. The default command opens an interactive picker; <code>codex cloud exec</code> submits a task directly, and <code>codex cloud list</code> returns recent chats for scripting or quick inspection.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>cloudExecOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Authentication follows the same credentials as the main CLI. Codex exits non-zero if the task submission fails.</p> <h4 id=\"codex-cloud-list\"><code>codex cloud list</code></h4> <p>List recent cloud chats with optional filtering and pagination.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>cloudListOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Plain-text output prints a task URL followed by status details. Use <code>--json</code> for automation. The JSON payload contains a <code>tasks</code> array plus an optional <code>cursor</code> value. Each task includes <code>id</code>, <code>url</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>updated_at</code>, <code>environment_id</code>, <code>environment_label</code>, <code>summary</code>, <code>is_review</code>, and <code>attempt_total</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-completion\"><code>codex completion</code></h3> <p>Generate shell completion scripts and redirect the output to the appropriate location, for example <code>codex completion zsh &gt; \"${fpath[1]}/_codex\"</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>completionOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-doctor\"><code>codex doctor</code></h3> <p>Generate a local diagnostic report before filing a support issue or while investigating a broken Codex installation. The report checks installation, configuration, authentication, runtime, Git, terminal, app-server, and thread inventory health.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>doctorOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-features\"><code>codex features</code></h3> <p>Manage feature flags stored in <code>$CODEX_HOME/config.toml</code>. The <code>enable</code> and <code>disable</code> commands persist changes so they apply to future sessions. The <code>features</code> subcommand doesn't accept <code>--profile</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>featuresOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-exec\"><code>codex exec</code></h3> <p>Use <code>codex exec</code> (or the short form <code>codex e</code>) for scripted or CI-style runs that should finish without human interaction.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>execOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Codex writes formatted output by default. Add <code>--json</code> to receive newline-delimited JSON events (one per state change). The optional <code>resume</code> subcommand lets you continue non-interactive tasks. Use <code>--last</code> to pick the most recent session from the current working directory, or add <code>--all</code> to search across all sessions:</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>execResumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>codex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; [PROMPT]</code> to copy a saved session into a new session. The session argument accepts a UUID or name. With no prompt, Codex creates the fork without starting a turn. Pass <code>-</code> as the prompt to read it from stdin, or add <code>--image</code> to attach images.</p> <p>A prompt is required when using images, <code>--output-schema</code>, <code>--output-last-message</code>, or <code>--ephemeral</code>.</p> <p>Add <code>--worktree</code> to a new or forked run to create a managed Git worktree:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">codex exec --worktree \"implement the next step\"\ncodex exec fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree \"try an alternative approach\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>--worktree</code> requires local execution. Don't combine it with <code>resume</code>, <code>review</code>, <code>--ephemeral</code>, or <code>--ignore-user-config</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-execpolicy\"><code>codex execpolicy</code></h3> <p>Check <code>execpolicy</code> rule files before you save them. <code>codex execpolicy check</code> accepts one or more <code>--rules</code> flags (for example, files under <code>~/.codex/rules</code>) and emits JSON showing the strictest decision and any matching rules. Add <code>--pretty</code> to format the output. The <code>execpolicy</code> command is currently in preview.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>execpolicyOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-login\"><code>codex login</code></h3> <p>Authenticate the CLI with a ChatGPT account, API key, or access token. With no flags, Codex opens a browser for the ChatGPT OAuth flow.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>loginOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex login status</code> exits with <code>0</code> when credentials are present, which is helpful in automation scripts.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-logout\"><code>codex logout</code></h3> <p>Remove saved credentials for both API key and ChatGPT authentication. This command has no flags.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp\"><code>codex mcp</code></h3> <p>Manage Model Context Protocol server entries stored in <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>mcpCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p>The <code>add</code> subcommand supports both stdio and streamable HTTP transports:</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>mcpAddOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>OAuth actions (<code>login</code>, <code>logout</code>) only work with streamable HTTP servers (and only when the server supports OAuth).</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin\"><code>codex plugin</code></h3> <p>Install, list, and remove plugins from configured marketplaces.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>pluginCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin add --json</code> prints <code>pluginId</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>marketplaceName</code>, <code>version</code>, <code>installedPath</code>, and <code>authPolicy</code>. <code>codex plugin list --json</code> prints <code>installed</code> and <code>available</code> arrays. Entries include <code>pluginId</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>marketplaceName</code>, <code>version</code>, <code>installed</code>, <code>enabled</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>installPolicy</code>, <code>authPolicy</code>, and, when available, <code>marketplaceSource</code> with the configured marketplace source type and value. <code>codex plugin remove --json</code> prints <code>pluginId</code>, <code>name</code>, and <code>marketplaceName</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-plugin-marketplace\"><code>codex plugin marketplace</code></h3> <p>Manage plugin marketplace sources that Codex can browse and install from.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>marketplaceCommands</code></p> </blockquote> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace add</code> accepts GitHub shorthand such as <code>owner/repo</code> or <code>owner/repo@ref</code>, HTTP or HTTPS Git URLs, SSH Git URLs, and local marketplace root directories. Use <code>--ref</code> to pin a Git ref, and repeat <code>--sparse PATH</code> to use a sparse checkout for Git-backed marketplace repositories.</p> <p><code>codex plugin marketplace list</code> prints in-scope marketplace names and roots, including implicitly discovered default marketplaces and configured marketplace snapshots.</p> <p>Add <code>--json</code> to marketplace add, list, upgrade, or remove commands for automation-friendly output. Marketplace add JSON includes <code>marketplaceName</code>, <code>installedRoot</code>, and <code>alreadyAdded</code>; list JSON includes a <code>marketplaces</code> array with <code>name</code>, <code>root</code>, and optional <code>marketplaceSource</code>; upgrade JSON includes <code>selectedMarketplaces</code>, <code>upgradedRoots</code>, and <code>errors</code>; remove JSON includes <code>marketplaceName</code> and <code>installedRoot</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-mcp-server\"><code>codex mcp-server</code></h3> <p>The <code>codex mcp-server</code> command and standalone <code>codex-mcp-server</code> binary have been removed. Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app server</a> instead.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-resume\"><code>codex resume</code></h3> <p>Continue an interactive session by ID or resume the most recent chat. <code>codex resume</code> scopes <code>--last</code> to the current working directory unless you pass <code>--all</code>. It accepts model and sandbox overrides, but not <code>--worktree</code>.</p> <p>If the current working directory differs from the session's saved directory, Codex asks which directory to use. Set <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\"><code>tui.resume_cwd</code></a> to <code>\"current\"</code> or <code>\"session\"</code> to reuse that choice without a prompt. An explicit <code>--cd</code> (<code>-C</code>) override takes precedence over <code>tui.resume_cwd</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>resumeOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-fork\"><code>codex fork</code></h3> <p>Fork a previous interactive session into a new chat. By default, <code>codex fork</code> opens the session picker; add <code>--last</code> to fork your most recent session instead.</p> <p>When the current and saved session directories differ, <code>codex fork</code> uses the same working-directory prompt and <code>tui.resume_cwd</code> setting as <code>codex resume</code>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>forkOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p>To fork into a managed Git worktree, run <code>codex fork &lt;SESSION_ID&gt; --worktree</code>. This requires an explicit session ID and local execution; it doesn't support <code>--last</code> or the session picker.</p> <h3 id=\"codex-sandbox\"><code>codex sandbox</code></h3> <p>Use the sandbox helper to run a command under the same policies Codex uses internally.</p> <h4 id=\"macos-seatbelt\">macOS seatbelt</h4> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>sandboxMacOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"linux-landlock\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"linux-sandbox\">Linux sandbox</h4> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>sandboxLinuxOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h4 id=\"windows\">Windows</h4> <blockquote> <p>Configuration-table data reference: <code>sandboxWindowsOptions</code></p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"codex-update\"><code>codex update</code></h3> <p>Check for and apply a Codex CLI update when the installed release supports self-update. Debug builds print a message telling you to install a release build instead.</p> <h2 id=\"flag-combinations-and-safety-tips\">Flag combinations and safety tips</h2> <ul> <li>Use <code>--sandbox workspace-write</code> for unattended local work that can stay inside the workspace, and avoid <code>--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox</code> unless you are inside a dedicated sandbox VM.</li> <li>When you need to grant Codex write access to more directories, prefer <code>--add-dir</code> rather than forcing <code>--sandbox danger-full-access</code>.</li> <li>Pair <code>--json</code> with <code>--output-last-message</code> in CI to capture machine-readable progress and a final natural-language summary.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"interactive-shortcuts\">Interactive shortcuts</h2> <ul> <li>Type <code>@</code> to search for a file in the workspace and add its path to the prompt.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Up</kbd> or <kbd>Down</kbd> to restore draft history.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> to search prompt history, then press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to use a match or <kbd>Escape</kbd> to cancel.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> or run <code>/copy</code> to copy the latest completed Codex output.</li> <li>Prefix a line with <code>!</code> to run a local shell command under the current approval and sandbox settings.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Tab</kbd> while Codex is working to queue a follow-up prompt, slash command, or shell command for the next turn.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> while Codex is working to inject new instructions into the current turn.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Escape</kbd> twice with an empty composer to edit the previous user message and fork the chat from that point.</li> <li>Press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd> or run <code>/exit</code> to close the session.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"related-resources\">Related resources</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI overview</a>: installation, upgrades, and quick tips.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>: persist defaults like the model and provider.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">Advanced Config</a>: profiles, providers, sandbox tuning, and integrations.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a>: conceptual overview of Codex agent capabilities and best practices.</li> </ul> <p>Slash commands give you fast, keyboard-first control over Codex. Type <code>/</code> in the composer to open the slash popup, choose a command, and Codex will perform actions such as switching models, adjusting permissions, or summarizing long chats without leaving the terminal.</p> <p>This guide shows you how to:</p> <ul> <li>Find the right built-in slash command for a task</li> <li>Steer an active session with commands like <code>/model</code>, <code>/fast</code>, <code>/permissions</code>, <code>/approve</code>, <code>/raw</code>, <code>/agents</code>, <code>/subagents</code>, and <code>/status</code></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"built-in-slash-commands\">Built-in slash commands</h2> <p>Codex ships with the following commands. Open the slash popup and start typing the command name to filter the list.</p> <p>When a chat is already running, you can type a slash command and press <code>Tab</code> to queue it for the next turn. Codex parses queued slash commands when they run, so command menus and errors appear after the current turn finishes. Slash completion still works before you queue the command.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Command</th> <th>Purpose</th> <th>When to use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=update-permissions-with-permissions\"><code>/permissions</code></a></td> <td>Set what Codex can do without asking first.</td> <td>Relax or tighten approval requirements mid-session, such as switching between Auto and Read Only.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=include-ide-context-with-ide\"><code>/ide</code></a></td> <td>Include open files, current selection, and other IDE context.</td> <td>Pull editor context into the next prompt without re-explaining what's open in your IDE.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\"><code>/keymap</code></a></td> <td>Remap TUI keyboard shortcuts.</td> <td>Inspect and persist custom shortcut bindings in <code>config.toml</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\"><code>/vim</code></a></td> <td>Toggle Vim mode for the composer.</td> <td>Switch between Vim normal/insert behavior and the default composer editing mode.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\"><code>/setup-default-sandbox</code></a></td> <td>Set up the elevated agent sandbox (Windows only).</td> <td>Replace the degraded Windows sandbox after Codex offers the elevated setup.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=manage-chats-with-agents\"><code>/agents</code></a></td> <td>Open the agent command center.</td> <td>Browse chats and switch between agents on the connected server.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\"><code>/subagents</code></a></td> <td>Switch the active subagent thread.</td> <td>Inspect or continue work in a subagent from the current session.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=browse-apps-with-apps\"><code>/apps</code></a></td> <td>Browse apps (connectors) and insert them into your prompt.</td> <td>Attach an app as <code>$app-slug</code> before asking Codex to use it.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=browse-plugins-with-plugins\"><code>/plugins</code></a></td> <td>Browse installed and discoverable plugins.</td> <td>Inspect plugin tools, install suggested plugins, or manage plugin availability.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\"><code>/hooks</code></a></td> <td>View and manage lifecycle hooks.</td> <td>Inspect configured hooks, trust new or changed hooks, or disable non-managed hooks before they run.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"><code>/clear</code></a></td> <td>Clear the terminal and start a fresh chat.</td> <td>Reset the visible UI and chat context together when you want a fresh start.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"><code>/rename</code></a></td> <td>Rename the current chat.</td> <td>Give a saved session a recognizable name without leaving the TUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=archive-the-current-session-with-archive\"><code>/archive</code></a></td> <td>Archive the current session.</td> <td>Remove the current session from active session lists without deleting its transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=delete-the-current-session-with-delete\"><code>/delete</code></a></td> <td>Permanently delete the current session.</td> <td>Remove the transcript and descendant sessions when archiving isn't enough.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\"><code>/compact</code></a></td> <td>Summarize the visible chat to free tokens.</td> <td>Use after long runs so Codex retains key points without blowing the context window.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\"><code>/copy</code></a></td> <td>Copy the latest completed Codex output.</td> <td>Grab the latest finished response or plan text without manually selecting it. You can also press <code>Ctrl+O</code>.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=review-changes-with-diff\"><code>/diff</code></a></td> <td>Show the Git diff, including files Git isn't tracking yet.</td> <td>Review Codex's edits before you commit or run tests.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/exit</code></a></td> <td>Exit the CLI (same as <code>/quit</code>).</td> <td>Alternative spelling; both commands exit the session.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\"><code>/experimental</code></a></td> <td>Toggle experimental features.</td> <td>Enable options such as Network proxy or Prevent sleep while running.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\"><code>/approve</code></a></td> <td>Approve one retry of a recent auto review denial.</td> <td>Retry a command or action that the auto reviewer denied.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=configure-memories-with-memories\"><code>/memories</code></a></td> <td>Configure memory use and generation.</td> <td>Turn memory injection or memory generation on or off without leaving the TUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=use-skills-with-skills\"><code>/skills</code></a></td> <td>Browse and use skills.</td> <td>Improve task-specific behavior by selecting a relevant local skill.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\"><code>/import</code></a></td> <td>Import Claude Code or Cursor setup, projects, and chats.</td> <td>Migrate supported external-agent artifacts into Codex configuration and local files.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=send-feedback-with-feedback\"><code>/feedback</code></a></td> <td>Send logs to the Codex maintainers.</td> <td>Report issues or share diagnostics with support.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=generate-agentsmd-with-init\"><code>/init</code></a></td> <td>Generate an <code>AGENTS.md</code> scaffold in the current directory.</td> <td>Capture persistent instructions for the repository or subdirectory you're working in.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=sign-out-with-logout\"><code>/logout</code></a></td> <td>Sign out of Codex.</td> <td>Clear local credentials when using a shared machine.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\"><code>/mcp</code></a></td> <td>List configured Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools.</td> <td>Check which external tools Codex can call during the session; add <code>verbose</code> for server details.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=highlight-files-with-mention\"><code>/mention</code></a></td> <td>Attach a file to the chat.</td> <td>Point Codex at specific files or folders you want it to inspect next.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=set-the-active-model-with-model\"><code>/model</code></a></td> <td>Choose the active model (and reasoning effort, when available).</td> <td>Use <code>gpt-6-luna</code> or <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> if shown.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\"><code>/fast</code></a></td> <td>Toggle a Fast service tier when the model catalog exposes one.</td> <td>Turn the current model's Fast tier on or off and persist the selection.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\"><code>/plan</code></a></td> <td>Switch to plan mode and optionally send a prompt.</td> <td>Ask Codex to propose an execution plan before implementation work starts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\"><code>/goal</code></a></td> <td>Set, edit, pause, resume, view, or clear a task goal.</td> <td>Give Codex a persistent target to track while a larger task runs.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=check-background-terminals-with-ps\"><code>/ps</code></a></td> <td>Show background terminals and their recent output.</td> <td>Check long-running commands without leaving the main transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=stop-background-terminals-with-stop\"><code>/stop</code></a></td> <td>Stop all background terminals.</td> <td>Cancel background terminal work started by the current session.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\"><code>/fork</code></a></td> <td>Fork the current chat into a new chat.</td> <td>Branch the active session to explore a new approach without losing the current transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\"><code>/app</code></a></td> <td>Continue the current session in the ChatGPT desktop app.</td> <td>Move from the TUI to the desktop app on macOS or Windows.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=start-a-side-chat-with-side\"><code>/side</code>, <code>/btw</code></a></td> <td>Start an ephemeral side chat.</td> <td>Ask a focused follow-up without disrupting the main chat's transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\"><code>/raw</code></a></td> <td>Toggle raw scrollback mode.</td> <td>Make terminal selection and copying less formatted while reviewing long output.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\"><code>/resume</code></a></td> <td>Resume a saved chat from your session list.</td> <td>Continue work from a previous CLI session without starting over.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=start-a-new-chat-with-new\"><code>/new</code></a></td> <td>Start a new chat inside the same CLI session.</td> <td>Reset the chat context without leaving the CLI when you want a fresh prompt in the same repo.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\"><code>/quit</code></a></td> <td>Exit the CLI.</td> <td>Leave the session immediately.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\"><code>/review</code></a></td> <td>Ask Codex to review your working tree.</td> <td>Run after Codex completes work or when you want a second set of eyes on local changes.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=inspect-the-session-with-status\"><code>/status</code></a></td> <td>Display session configuration and token usage.</td> <td>Confirm the active model, approval policy, writable roots, and remaining context capacity.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=view-account-usage-with-usage\"><code>/usage</code></a></td> <td>View account token usage or use a rate-limit reset.</td> <td>Inspect daily, weekly, or cumulative ChatGPT token activity from inside the TUI.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\"><code>/debug-config</code></a></td> <td>Print config layer and requirements diagnostics.</td> <td>Debug precedence and policy requirements, including experimental network constraints.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=configure-footer-items-with-statusline\"><code>/statusline</code></a></td> <td>Configure TUI status-line fields interactively.</td> <td>Pick and reorder footer items (model/context/limits/git/tokens/session) and persist in config.toml.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\"><code>/title</code></a></td> <td>Configure terminal window or tab title fields interactively.</td> <td>Pick and reorder title items such as project, status, thread, branch, model, and task progress.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\"><code>/theme</code></a></td> <td>Choose a syntax-highlighting theme.</td> <td>Preview and persist a terminal syntax-highlighting theme.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\"><code>/pets</code>, <code>/pet</code></a></td> <td>Choose or hide a terminal pet.</td> <td>Personalize the TUI with a built-in or custom ambient pet.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\"><code>/tui</code></a></td> <td>Choose the terminal mode for the next launch.</td> <td>Switch between terminal scrollback and a fullscreen transcript.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=export-a-conversation-with-export\"><code>/export</code></a></td> <td>Export the conversation as Markdown.</td> <td>Save a complete transcript to a file or copy it to the clipboard.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=summarize-the-chat-with-recap\"><code>/recap</code></a></td> <td>Generate a summary of the current conversation.</td> <td>Catch up on the chat without compacting its context.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/cd</code></a></td> <td>Change the session's working directory.</td> <td>Continue an idle primary chat in another directory.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=change-directories-with-cd\"><code>/pwd</code>, <code>/cwd</code></a></td> <td>Show the working directory.</td> <td>Check the directory the active session uses.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\"><code>/worktree</code></a></td> <td>Start or continue a chat in a managed Git worktree.</td> <td>Work in a separate checkout of a local repository.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\"><code>/daemon</code></a></td> <td>Open background server controls.</td> <td>Inspect the connection and manage a local server owned by Codex.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"#/article/a-cf38bd5054bede68?anchor=inspect-warnings-with-warnings\"><code>/warnings</code></a></td> <td>View retained warnings and diagnostics.</td> <td>Revisit warnings that appeared during the session.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><code>/quit</code> and <code>/exit</code> both exit the CLI. Use them only after you have saved or committed any important work.</p> <p>Use <code>/permissions</code> to adjust what Codex can do without asking first. Use <code>/approve</code> only when you need to retry a recent action that automatic review denied.</p> <h2 id=\"control-your-session-with-slash-commands\">Control your session with slash commands</h2> <p>The following workflows keep your session on track without restarting Codex.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-the-terminal-mode-with-tui\">Choose the terminal mode with <code>/tui</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/tui</code>.</li> <li>Choose scrollback or fullscreen mode, then confirm.</li> <li>Restart Codex to apply the selection.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: The next launch uses the saved terminal mode. Launch overrides such as <code>--no-alt-screen</code> still apply.</p> <h3 id=\"export-a-conversation-with-export\">Export a conversation with <code>/export</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/export</code>.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Copy to clipboard</strong> or <strong>Save to file</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex exports the complete conversation as Markdown. To save directly to a file, run <code>/export session.md</code>. Wait for the current turn to finish before exporting.</p> <h3 id=\"summarize-the-chat-with-recap\">Summarize the chat with <code>/recap</code></h3> <ol> <li>When Codex is idle, type <code>/recap</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex generates a summary of the conversation, even if <code>tui.auto_recap = false</code>. Use <code>/compact</code> when you want to free context space.</p> <h3 id=\"change-directories-with-cd\">Change directories with <code>/cd</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/pwd</code> (or <code>/cwd</code>) to check the current directory.</li> <li>Type <code>/cd &lt;path&gt;</code> to change directories, or <code>/cd</code> to use your home directory.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex continues the chat in the selected directory. Changing directories requires an idle primary session with no queued input or background terminals.</p> <h3 id=\"continue-in-a-worktree-with-worktree\">Continue in a worktree with <code>/worktree</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/worktree</code> in a local Git repository.</li> <li>Choose whether to start a new chat or continue the current conversation in a new worktree.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex creates a managed Git worktree and starts the selected chat there. Choose <strong>Browse worktrees</strong> to find existing worktrees and their owner chats. This command requires local worktree support and is unavailable while a task is running.</p> <h3 id=\"manage-the-background-server-with-daemon\">Manage the background server with <code>/daemon</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/daemon</code>.</li> <li>Review the server connection and available actions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex offers to install the latest public stable release or use the current CLI build for the local background server. Confirming an update exits Codex and may interrupt active work. For a remote connection, manage the server on its host.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-warnings-with-warnings\">Inspect warnings with <code>/warnings</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/warnings</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows retained warnings and their diagnostic details.</p> <h3 id=\"set-the-active-model-with-model\">Set the active model with <code>/model</code></h3> <p>The picker only shows models available to your account and workspace. If GPT-6.1 Sol isn't listed, choose another model. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol availability by plan</a>.</p> <ol> <li>Start Codex and open the composer.</li> <li>Type <code>/model</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Choose a model such as <code>gpt-6-luna</code> or <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> from the popup.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex confirms the new model in the transcript. Run <code>/status</code> to verify the change.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-fast-mode-with-fast\">Toggle Fast mode with <code>/fast</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/fast</code> to turn the current model's Fast service tier on.</li> <li>Type <code>/fast</code> again to turn it off.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex toggles the tier and saves the selection. In the TUI footer, you can also show a Fast mode status-line item with <code>/statusline</code>.</p> <p>Fast tier commands are catalog-driven. If the current model doesn't advertise a Fast tier, Codex won't show <code>/fast</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"switch-to-plan-mode-with-plan\">Switch to plan mode with <code>/plan</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/plan</code> and press Enter to switch the active chat into plan mode.</li> <li>Optional: provide inline prompt text (for example, <code>/plan Propose a\nmigration plan for this service</code>).</li> <li>You can paste content or attach images while using inline <code>/plan</code> arguments.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex enters plan mode and uses your optional inline prompt as the first planning request.</p> <p>While Codex is already working, <code>/plan</code> is temporarily unavailable.</p> <h3 id=\"set-or-view-a-task-goal-with-goal\">Set or view a task goal with <code>/goal</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/goal &lt;objective&gt;</code> to set the goal, for example <code>/goal Finish the migration and keep tests green</code>.</li> <li>Type <code>/goal</code> to view the current goal.</li> <li>Use <code>/goal edit</code> to revise the objective. Use <code>/goal pause</code>, <code>/goal resume</code>, or <code>/goal clear</code> to pause, resume, or remove it.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex keeps the goal attached to the active chat while work continues.</p> <p>Goal objectives must be non-empty and at most 4,000 characters. For longer instructions, put the details in a file and point the goal at that file.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-experimental-features-with-experimental\">Toggle experimental features with <code>/experimental</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/experimental</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Toggle the features you want (for example, Network proxy or Prevent sleep while running), then restart Codex if the prompt asks you to.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex saves your feature choices to config and applies them on restart.</p> <h3 id=\"approve-an-auto-review-denial-with-approve\">Approve an auto review denial with <code>/approve</code></h3> <p>Use <code>/approve</code> when the automatic reviewer denied a recent action and you want Codex to retry it once.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/approve</code>.</li> <li>Confirm the retry when Codex shows the relevant denied action.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex retries that denied action once under the current session policy.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-memories-with-memories\">Configure memories with <code>/memories</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/memories</code>.</li> <li>Choose whether Codex should use existing memories, generate new memories, or keep memory behavior disabled.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates the relevant memory settings for future sessions.</p> <h3 id=\"use-skills-with-skills\">Use skills with <code>/skills</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/skills</code>.</li> <li>Pick the skill you want Codex to apply.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex inserts the selected skill context so the next request follows that skill's instructions.</p> <p><a id=\"import-claude-code-configuration-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a> <a id=\"cli-import-claude-code-setup-with-import\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"import-claude-code-or-cursor-setup-with-import\">Import Claude Code or Cursor setup with <code>/import</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/import</code>.</li> <li>Choose <strong>Claude Code</strong> or <strong>Cursor</strong>.</li> <li>Select the setup, project files, or recent chats you want to migrate.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens the external-agent import picker and imports the selected supported artifacts into Codex configuration and local files. Session discovery includes up to 50 chats from the last 30 days.</p> <p>Run <code>/import</code> from a local TUI session. It's unavailable while a task is running, in remote sessions, and while connected to the local app-server daemon.</p> <p>For the desktop app workflow and supported artifact types, see <a href=\"#/article/a-2b09a0f3c8670621\">Import from another agent</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\"></a> <a id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-task-with-clear\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"clear-the-terminal-and-start-a-new-chat-with-clear\">Clear the terminal and start a new chat with <code>/clear</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/clear</code> and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex clears the terminal, resets the visible transcript, and starts a fresh chat in the same CLI session.</p> <p>To name the new chat as you create it, run <code>/clear release prep</code>.</p> <p>Unlike <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd>, <code>/clear</code> starts a new chat.</p> <p><kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>L</kbd> only clears the terminal view and keeps the current chat. Codex disables both actions while a task is in progress.</p> <h3 id=\"archive-the-current-session-with-archive\">Archive the current session with <code>/archive</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/archive</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Confirm that you want to archive the current session.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex archives the session and returns to the command center when connected to a local background server or remote server. Without a shared server, Codex exits. Codex keeps the transcript; restore it later with <code>codex unarchive &lt;SESSION&gt;</code>.</p> <p>If a turn is running, confirming <code>/archive</code> stops that turn before archiving.</p> <h3 id=\"delete-the-current-session-with-delete\">Delete the current session with <code>/delete</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/delete</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Confirm that you want to delete the current session.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex permanently deletes the transcript and spawned descendant sessions. When connected to a local background server or remote server, Codex returns to the command center. Without a shared server, Codex exits.</p> <p><code>/delete</code> is unavailable while a chat is running or in a side chat.</p> <h3 id=\"update-permissions-with-permissions\">Update permissions with <code>/permissions</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/permissions</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Select the approval preset that matches your comfort level, for example <code>Auto</code> for hands-off runs or <code>Read Only</code> to review edits. When named permission profiles are active, the picker also shows configured custom profiles and their descriptions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex announces the updated policy. Future actions respect the updated approval mode until you change it again.</p> <h3 id=\"include-ide-context-with-ide\">Include IDE context with <code>/ide</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/ide</code>.</li> <li>Add optional inline text if you want to explain what Codex should do with the current IDE selection or open files.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex includes available IDE context in the next prompt.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-vim-mode-with-vim\">Toggle Vim mode with <code>/vim</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/vim</code>.</li> <li>Continue editing in the composer.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex toggles composer Vim mode for the current session. To make Vim mode the default for new sessions, set <code>tui.vim_mode_default = true</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"set-up-the-elevated-windows-sandbox-with-setup-default-sandbox\">Set up the elevated Windows sandbox with <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code></h3> <p>This command appears only on Windows when Codex is using the degraded restricted-token sandbox.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/setup-default-sandbox</code>.</li> <li>Follow the administrator setup flow.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex configures the elevated Windows sandbox and selects the corresponding automatic approval preset.</p> <h3 id=\"copy-the-latest-response-with-copy\">Copy the latest response with <code>/copy</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/copy</code> and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex copies the latest completed Codex output to your clipboard.</p> <p>If a turn is still running, <code>/copy</code> uses the latest completed output instead of the in-progress response. The command is unavailable before the first completed Codex output and immediately after a rollback.</p> <p>You can also press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>O</kbd> from the main TUI to copy the latest completed response without opening the slash command menu.</p> <h3 id=\"toggle-raw-scrollback-with-raw\">Toggle raw scrollback with <code>/raw</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/raw</code>, <code>/raw on</code>, or <code>/raw off</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex toggles raw scrollback mode, which makes terminal selection and copying more direct. You can also use the default <kbd>Alt</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> binding or persist the default with <code>tui.raw_output_mode = true</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-the-session-with-status\">Inspect the session with <code>/status</code></h3> <ol> <li>In any chat, type <code>/status</code>.</li> <li>Review the output for the active model, approval policy, writable roots, and current token usage. When the TUI connects remotely, the output also shows the remote address and the server version.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex prints a summary confirming that it's operating where you expect.</p> <h3 id=\"view-account-usage-with-usage\">View account usage with <code>/usage</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/usage</code> to open the usage menu.</li> <li>Choose whether to show token activity or redeem an available earned reset.</li> <li>To open token activity directly, type <code>/usage daily</code>, <code>/usage weekly</code>, or <code>/usage cumulative</code>.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens usage actions or shows account token activity for the selected view. If the session doesn't have Codex service account auth, Codex shows a sign-in requirement.</p> <h3 id=\"inspect-config-layers-with-debug-config\">Inspect config layers with <code>/debug-config</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/debug-config</code>.</li> <li>Review the output for config layer order (lowest precedence first), on/off state, and policy sources.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex prints layer diagnostics plus policy details such as <code>allowed_approval_policies</code>, <code>allowed_sandbox_modes</code>, <code>mcp_servers</code>, <code>rules</code>, and <code>experimental_network</code> when configured.</p> <p>Use this output to debug why an effective setting differs from <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-footer-items-with-statusline\">Configure footer items with <code>/statusline</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/statusline</code>.</li> <li>Use the picker to toggle and reorder items, then confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: The footer status line updates immediately and persists to <code>tui.status_line</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <p>Available status-line items include model, model+reasoning, context stats, rate limits, git branch, token counters, session id, current directory/project root, and Codex version.</p> <h3 id=\"configure-terminal-title-items-with-title\">Configure terminal title items with <code>/title</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/title</code>.</li> <li>Use the picker to toggle and reorder items, then confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: The terminal window or tab title updates immediately and persists to <code>tui.terminal_title</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <p>Available title items include app name, project, spinner, status, thread, git branch, model, and task progress.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-a-syntax-theme-with-theme\">Choose a syntax theme with <code>/theme</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/theme</code>.</li> <li>Preview a theme from the picker, then confirm.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates syntax highlighting and persists the choice to <code>tui.theme</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"choose-a-terminal-pet-with-pets\">Choose a terminal pet with <code>/pets</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/pets</code> (or <code>/pet</code>) to open the pet picker.</li> <li>Choose a built-in or custom pet, or turn pets off.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex displays the selected ambient pet in supported terminals and persists the selection. You can also type <code>/pets off</code> to hide it.</p> <h3 id=\"remap-tui-shortcuts-with-keymap\">Remap TUI shortcuts with <code>/keymap</code></h3> <p>Use <code>/keymap</code> to inspect, update, and persist keyboard shortcut bindings for the TUI.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/keymap</code>.</li> <li>Pick the shortcut context and action you want to change.</li> <li>Enter the new binding or remove the existing one.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates the active keymap and writes the custom binding to <code>tui.keymap</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <p>Key bindings use names such as <code>ctrl-a</code>, <code>shift-enter</code>, and <code>page-down</code>. Context-specific bindings override <code>tui.keymap.global</code>; an empty binding list unbinds the action.</p> <h3 id=\"check-background-terminals-with-ps\">Check background terminals with <code>/ps</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/ps</code>.</li> <li>Review the list of background terminals and their status.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows each background terminal's command plus up to three recent, non-empty output lines so you can gauge progress at a glance.</p> <p>Background terminals appear when <code>unified_exec</code> is in use; otherwise, the list may be empty.</p> <h3 id=\"stop-background-terminals-with-stop\">Stop background terminals with <code>/stop</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/stop</code>.</li> <li>Confirm if Codex asks before stopping the listed terminals.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex stops all background terminals for the current session. <code>/clean</code> is still available as an alias for <code>/stop</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-transcripts-lean-with-compact\">Keep transcripts lean with <code>/compact</code></h3> <ol> <li>After a long exchange, type <code>/compact</code>.</li> <li>Confirm when Codex offers to summarize the chat so far.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex replaces earlier turns with a concise summary, freeing context while keeping critical details.</p> <h3 id=\"review-changes-with-diff\">Review changes with <code>/diff</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/diff</code> to inspect the Git diff.</li> <li>Scroll through the output inside the CLI to review edits and added files.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows changes you've staged, changes you haven't staged yet, and files Git hasn't started tracking, so you can decide what to keep.</p> <h3 id=\"highlight-files-with-mention\">Highlight files with <code>/mention</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/mention</code> followed by a path, for example <code>/mention src/lib/api.ts</code>.</li> <li>Select the matching result from the popup.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex adds the file to the chat, ensuring follow-up turns reference it directly.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-new-conversation-with-new\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"start-a-new-chat-with-new\">Start a new chat with <code>/new</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/new</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>If Codex offers a checkout choice, choose the current directory or a new worktree.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex starts a fresh chat in the same CLI session, so you can switch chats without leaving your terminal.</p> <p>To name the new chat as you create it, run <code>/new bug bash</code>.</p> <p>Unlike <code>/clear</code>, <code>/new</code> doesn't clear the current terminal view first.</p> <p><a id=\"rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\"></a> <a id=\"rename-the-current-task-with-rename\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"rename-the-current-chat-with-rename\">Rename the current chat with <code>/rename</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/rename &lt;name&gt;</code>, or type <code>/rename</code> to open the naming prompt.</li> <li>Enter a short name that will help you find the chat later.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex updates the saved chat name without changing its transcript.</p> <p><a id=\"resume-a-saved-conversation-with-resume\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"resume-a-saved-chat-with-resume\">Resume a saved chat with <code>/resume</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/resume</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Choose the session you want from the saved-session picker.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex reloads the selected chat's transcript so you can pick up where you left off, keeping the original history intact.</p> <p><a id=\"fork-the-current-conversation-with-fork\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"fork-the-current-chat-with-fork\">Fork the current chat with <code>/fork</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/fork</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>If Codex offers a checkout choice, choose the current directory or a new worktree.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex clones the current chat into a new chat with a fresh ID, leaving the original transcript untouched so you can explore an alternative approach in parallel.</p> <p>If you need to fork a saved session instead of the current one, run <code>codex fork</code> in your terminal to open the session picker.</p> <h3 id=\"continue-in-the-desktop-app-with-app\">Continue in the desktop app with <code>/app</code></h3> <p>On macOS and Windows, type <code>/app</code> to open the current session in the ChatGPT desktop app. If the app isn't installed or running, Codex shows an error asking you to install or launch it.</p> <p>Expected: The desktop app opens the same saved chat so you can continue there.</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-side-conversation-with-side\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"start-a-side-chat-with-side\">Start a side chat with <code>/side</code></h3> <p>Use <code>/side</code> to start an ephemeral fork from the current chat without switching away from the main chat.</p> <ol> <li>Type <code>/side</code> to open a side chat.</li> <li>Optionally add inline text, for example <code>/side Check whether this plan has an obvious risk</code>.</li> <li>Return to the parent chat after the focused detour finishes.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens a side chat whose transcript is separate from the parent chat. While you are in side mode, the TUI continues to show the parent chat's status so you can see whether the main chat is still running.</p> <p><code>/side</code> is unavailable inside another side chat and during review mode.</p> <h3 id=\"generate-agentsmd-with-init\">Generate <code>AGENTS.md</code> with <code>/init</code></h3> <ol> <li>Run <code>/init</code> in the directory where you want Codex to look for persistent instructions.</li> <li>Review the generated <code>AGENTS.md</code>, then edit it to match your repository conventions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex creates an <code>AGENTS.md</code> scaffold you can refine and commit for future sessions.</p> <h3 id=\"ask-for-a-working-tree-review-with-review\">Ask for a working tree review with <code>/review</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/review</code>.</li> <li>Follow up with <code>/diff</code> if you want to inspect the exact file changes.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex summarizes issues it finds in your working tree, focusing on behavior changes and missing tests. It uses the current session model unless you set <code>review_model</code> in <code>config.toml</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"list-mcp-tools-with-mcp\">List MCP tools with <code>/mcp</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/mcp</code>.</li> <li>Review the list to confirm which MCP servers and tools are available.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: You see the configured Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools Codex can call in this session.</p> <p>Use <code>/mcp verbose</code> to include detailed server diagnostics. Use <code>/mcp login &lt;name&gt;</code> to sign in to a configured MCP server from the active session.</p> <h3 id=\"browse-apps-with-apps\">Browse apps with <code>/apps</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/apps</code>.</li> <li>Pick an app from the list.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex inserts the app mention into the composer as <code>$app-slug</code>, so you can immediately ask Codex to use it.</p> <h3 id=\"browse-plugins-with-plugins\">Browse plugins with <code>/plugins</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/plugins</code>.</li> <li>Choose a marketplace tab, then pick a plugin to inspect its capabilities or available actions.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens the plugin browser so you can review installed plugins, discoverable plugins that your configuration allows, and installed plugin state. Press <kbd>Space</kbd> on an installed plugin to toggle its enabled state.</p> <h3 id=\"view-and-manage-lifecycle-hooks-with-hooks\">View and manage lifecycle hooks with <code>/hooks</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/hooks</code>.</li> <li>Choose a hook event to inspect the matching handlers.</li> <li>Trust, disable, or re-enable non-managed hooks as needed.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex opens the hook browser so you can review configured lifecycle hooks. Managed hooks appear as managed and can't be disabled from the user hook browser.</p> <h3 id=\"manage-chats-with-agents\">Manage chats with <code>/agents</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/agents</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Select a chat from the command center to open it.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex shows an overview of chats on the connected server. You can inspect their status and switch between them. To open the command center directly from your terminal, run <code>codex agents</code>. The command center requires a shared local or remote server.</p> <p><a id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-agent\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"switch-agent-threads-with-subagents\">Switch agent threads with <code>/subagents</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/subagents</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Select the thread you want from the picker.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex switches the active thread so you can inspect or continue that agent's work.</p> <h3 id=\"send-feedback-with-feedback\">Send feedback with <code>/feedback</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/feedback</code> and press Enter.</li> <li>Follow the prompts to include logs or diagnostics.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex collects the requested diagnostics and submits them to the maintainers.</p> <h3 id=\"sign-out-with-logout\">Sign out with <code>/logout</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/logout</code> and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex clears local credentials for the current user session.</p> <h3 id=\"exit-the-cli-with-quit-or-exit\">Exit the CLI with <code>/quit</code> or <code>/exit</code></h3> <ol> <li>Type <code>/quit</code> (or <code>/exit</code>) and press Enter.</li> </ol> <p>Expected: Codex exits immediately. Save or commit any important work first.</p>"};
